entry='<article class="claim" id="source-work-v01"><div class="eyebrow">18 October 2026 UTC · Theorem milestone 0.1</div><h2>The endpoint contract now includes controlled source and defect work</h2><p>A shared cumulative budget admits varying positive norms, other parameter drift and continuous tangent implementation errors. A graph ground-energy bound shows that pure base norm loss adds no positive reference-energy work, although it can still generate Gauss charge.</p><p>The seven-page theorem derives the covariant Gauss-source law, a drift envelope, raw matter-force allocation and a sufficient constant-rate duration inequality. An exact control shows why zero terminal net work cannot replace an every-prefix bound. Forty-three exact checks and twelve matrix diagnostics pass. Independent review pending; physical promotion 0. No actual numerical trajectory, physical source sector or experimental dataset is certified by this milestone.</p><a class="text-link" href="/papers/#source-work-v01">Read the source and defect-work theorem →</a></article>'
